.TH RR2GRAPH 1 "May 2026" "rr2graph 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rr2graph \- visualize blood pressure, pulse and weight data from Excel files

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rr2graph
[\-e EXCEL]
[\-n NUM_OF_MONTHS]
[\-o OUTPUT]
[\-c CONFIG]
[\-g]
[\-i]
[\-v]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rr2graph
is a command-line tool that reads blood pressure, pulse and weight data from Excel files
and generates monthly visualizations.

It creates plots such as box-swarm, scatter, histogram and violin charts
and exports them as PNG, PDF and SVG files.

The tool can be used directly with command-line arguments or via a YAML configuration file.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e , \--excel " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to the Excel file containing measurement data.
Default: rr_data.xlsx

.TP
.BR \-n , \--num_of_months " " \fIN\fR
Number of months to visualize (typically 1–6).
Default: 3

.TP
.BR \-o , \--output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory for generated plots.
Default: plots/

.TP
.BR \-c , \--config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to optional YAML configuration file.
When provided, CLI arguments may be overridden by the config.
Default: config.yaml

.TP
.BR \-g , \--generate-test-data
Generate a sample Excel file (test_rr_data.xlsx) and exit.

.TP
.BR \-i , \--info
Show system information, configuration and environment details.

.TP
.BR \-v , \--version
Show program version and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
rr2graph supports an optional YAML configuration file.

Example:

.nf
excel: "rr_data.xlsx"
num_of_months: 3
output: "plots/"
.fi

If a configuration file is provided via \-c, its values may override CLI arguments.

.SH EXAMPLES
Run with default settings:

.nf
rr2graph
.fi

Use a custom Excel file:

.nf
rr2graph -e rr_data.xlsx -n 3 -o plots/
.fi

Generate test data:

.nf
rr2graph -g
.fi

Show system information:

.nf
rr2graph --info
.fi

Use a configuration file:

.nf
rr2graph -c config.yaml
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.yaml
Optional configuration file used to define input, output and processing settings.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
General error (invalid input, missing file, or configuration error).

